    "title": "Pelicot rebukes defendant from witness stand in rape appeal - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By DPA ,\n6 hours ago\nGisèle Pelicot reacted angrily on Wednesday towards the defendant in his appeal against raping her.\n\"You come through the door, when did I give you my consent? You rape me, two hours is a long time, I am ashamed of you,\" the Frechwoman said on the witness stand in the court in the southern city of Nîmes.\nIn the high-profile case, 50 men were sentenced late last year, mostly for rape, receiving prison terms ranging from three to 15 years.\nGisèle Pelicot's ex-husband, Dominique, admitted in court to drugging his then-wife repeatedly over nearly a decade, abusing her, and allowing strangers to rape her. He received the maximum sentence of 20 years in prison.\nInitially, 17 of those convicted planned to appeal, but only the 44-year-old defendant, who was sentenced to nine years in prison, has followed through.\nOn Wednesday, the appeals court reviewed video recordings made by Pelicot's ex-husband that show the alleged crime taking place. Many in the courtroom turned away.\nThe defendant denies the accusation of rape, claiming that Pelicot's ex-husband had told him she was only pretending to be asleep and that it was part of a game. He says he did not use violence.\nClosing arguments and a verdict in the appeal are expected on Thursday.\n1",
